PLACEHOLDER — the default Confidential AI module signing certificate goes here.

Generate the keypair per docs/module-signing.md, commit the resulting .crt over
this file, and store key+cert in the org-level MODULE_SIG_KEY_PEM secret.

This file is deliberately not a valid certificate: a build that reaches the
kernel's certs/system_certificates.S with this staged would fail confusingly,
so `confos kernel` rejects it up front instead.
